# PLACEHOLDER — replace this file with the real modprobed.db from your T480.
#
# This is deliberately not a real database. If you build against this file
# as-is, `make localmodconfig` will treat "no modules recorded" as "prune
# essentially everything" for any driver not explicitly forced back on by
# config/zenith.config. That fragment covers the T480's core hardware, but
# is not a substitute for a real, populated database.
#
# On the T480, generate a real one with:
#
#   sudo pacman -S modprobed-db        # Arch/CachyOS
#   # or build it from source: https://github.com/graysky2/modprobed-db
#
#   modprobed-db store                 # log every module ever probed
#   # use the machine normally for a while: suspend/resume, plug in USB
#   # devices, connect to Wi-Fi and Ethernet, use the webcam/fingerprint
#   # reader if applicable, etc., so the database actually reflects
#   # real usage.
#
# Then copy the resulting database (usually
# $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/modprobed.db or ~/.config/modprobed.db) to this path
# and commit it.
